PROPRIETARY LICENCE — Urban Digital Twin

================================================================================
1. WHAT THIS LICENCE COVERS
================================================================================

This licence covers, and covers only:

  (a) the PROJECT CODE in this repository — the source, configuration, scripts,
      tests and documentation authored for this project; and

  (b) the GENERATED ARTIFACTS produced by that code — the procedurally generated
      exterior geometry (glTF/GLB), the derived textures, the assembled release
      packages, tiles, indexes and the evidence records committed under `data/`.

All rights in (a) and (b) are reserved. No permission is granted to use, copy,
modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense or sell them, in whole or in
part, without the prior written permission of the copyright holder.

================================================================================
2. WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES *NOT* COVER — THIRD-PARTY SOURCE DATA
================================================================================

THIS LICENCE MAKES NO CLAIM OVER THIRD-PARTY SOURCE DATA.

The project ingests public and third-party datasets. Those datasets remain the
property of, and remain governed by the terms of, their respective sources. The
proprietary grant in section 1 does not extend to them, and nothing in this file
should be read as asserting ownership of, or as re-licensing, any of them.

This matters in both directions: some of the source data carries SHARE-ALIKE
obligations that a proprietary claim would contradict outright.

Carved out by name:

  (a) NYC OPEN DATA / NYC OFFICE OF TECHNOLOGY AND INNOVATION (OTI) DATASETS.
      Used under the NYC Open Data terms of use, and subject to the City's
      modified-data disclaimer. Includes the OTI Building Footprints dataset
      (jh45-qr5r) from which the exterior geometry is derived.
      Terms: <https://opendata.cityofnewyork.us/overview/> and
             <https://www.nyc.gov/html/datamine/html/data/terms.html?dataSetJs=raw>

  (b) THE ODbL 1.0 SHARE-ALIKE PARTITION — OpenStreetMap-derived data,
      including the block-835 commercial frontage metadata retained as a
      declared derivative-database partition, and Overture transportation data.
      Licensed under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0. Map data
      © OpenStreetMap contributors. ODbL 1.0 is a SHARE-ALIKE licence: the
      obligations attaching to that partition are not displaced by this file.
      Terms: <https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright>

  (c) CC BY-SA 4.0 PHOTOGRAPHIC REFERENCES from Wikimedia Commons, used as
      cited style references. CC BY-SA 4.0 is also a SHARE-ALIKE licence.
      Terms: <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/>

  (d) CITY OF NEW YORK PUBLICATION FACTS — registry licence class
      `nyc-publication-facts`: the LPC Flatiron designation report and the DCP
      Empire State design record. These are agency PUBLICATIONS rather than
      Open Data portal datasets, so they fall outside the literal wording of
      the NYC Open Data terms in (a) and are named separately.
      Terms: <https://www.nyc.gov/home/terms-of-use.page>

  (e) THIRD-PARTY SERVICES under their own provider terms (511NY, Google Places,
      Cesium Ion) and MTA open-data feeds.

  (f) SOURCES WHOSE LICENCE CLASS IS RECORDED AS `unknown` in the registry.
      They are used under the retention and local-only constraints recorded
      against them and carry no claim here.

The registry uses eight licence classes and the carve-outs above account for
six of them. The remaining two need no carve-out and are listed so the mapping
is exhaustive on its face: `public-domain` sources impose no obligation and are
not claimed here either, and `fixture-only` entries are locally synthesized
test data with no external source at all. A committed test fails if the
registry ever grows a licence class this file has not classified.

The authoritative, per-dataset list — every attribution string, terms URL and
licence class — is `src/data/source-registry.ts`, reproduced in `NOTICE`.
Where this file and that registry disagree, THE REGISTRY GOVERNS, and a
committed test asserts that `NOTICE` still agrees with it.

================================================================================
3. SCOPE OF USE ALREADY RECORDED
================================================================================

Redistribution and public-deployment posture is NOT granted by this file; it is
recorded per dataset in the source registry and in the approval evidence
committed alongside it. In particular, the 2026-08-11 authorization recorded
against `nyc.building-footprints` permits the GENERATED exterior geometry to be
publicly displayed, conveyed as a derivative and redistributed — with NYC OTI
attribution, the City modified-data disclaimer, source IDs, capture timestamp,
checksum, CRS and height uncertainty travelling with it — while the RAW
jh45-qr5r source dataset remains non-redistributable and public deployment
remains excluded. See `NOTICE` and `src/data/source-registry.ts`.

